📋 All possible process states

Here is the complete list of process states in Linux (from man ps):

State Name Meaning

R Running Running or runnable (on run queue)
S Sleeping Interruptible sleep (waiting for an event)
D Disk sleep Uninterruptible sleep (waiting for IO)
Z Zombie Process terminated, not reaped by parent
T Stopped Stopped by job control signal (SIGSTOP)
t Tracing stop Stopped by debugger
X Dead Should never appear (internal kernel state)
I Idle Kernel idle thread
K Wakekill Kill on wakeup
P Parked Parked by kernel
W Waking Waking up (Linux 2.6+)
< High priority High-priority process
N Low priority Low-priority process
L Has pages locked Pages locked into memory
s Session leader Process is a session leader
l Multi-threaded Process is multi-threaded
+ Foreground Running in foreground process group
✅ The most important ones for PostgreSQL troubleshooting are:

R, S, D, Z, T

🔥 The ones you must know

S
• Waiting for:
  • Network
  • Locks
  • Timers
  • User input
• Can be killed by signals
✅ Most PostgreSQL backends are usually S.

⚠️ D – Uninterruptible sleep (IO wait)
D
• Waiting for disk or storage
• Cannot be killed
• Cannot be interrupted

✅ Expected during:
• Autovacuum
• Checkpoints
• Large queries
• WAL writes

⚠️ Dangerous in large numbers or long duration.

🚨 Z – Zombie
Z
• Process finished
• Parent hasn’t read exit status
✅ Usually harmless unless many zombies accumulate.

🚨 T – Stopped
T
• Stopped by:
  • SIGSTOP
  • Debugger (gdb)
  • Job control (Ctrl+Z)

✅ Usually intentional.

🧪 Why grep ' D' works

This command:
ps -eo pid,state,cmd | grep ' D'

Finds:
• Any line where state column contains D
• That includes:
  • D
  • Ds (D + session leader)
  • DL (D + locked pages)

✅ It’s a safe, effective way to find IO-blocked processes.

✅ PostgreSQL-specific cheat sheet

Postgres process Typical state
Autovacuum worker D
Background writer S / D
Checkpointer D
User backend idle S
Active query R / S
Stuck backend D for long time ⚠️

✅ Final summary
✅ state = single-letter Linux process state  
✅ D = waiting for disk IO (uninterruptible)  
✅ S = normal sleep  
✅ R = running  
✅ Z = zombie  
✅ T = stopped  

